UPDATE companies SET description='AGT Foods USA operates its ingredient production facility in Minot, North Dakota, as part of the global AGT Food and Ingredients Inc. The company, majority owned by Fairfax Financial Holdings Limited, traces its roots to a mission of providing clean, quality pulses and foodstuffs with reliable shipments and competitive pricing. While a specific founding year is not disclosed, the guiding principle "From Producer to the World" has shaped its growth into a diversified food company.

The Minot facility is one of two North American ingredient plants (the other in Regina, Saskatchewan) that clean, size, split, colour-sort, and package pulses and grains. The company runs 39 manufacturing facilities across five continents, producing over 1,400 products including flours, proteins, starches, fibres, extruded texturized plant proteins, gluten-free pasta, wheat semolina, rice, and bulgur wheat. It also offers co-packing, custom blends, and private-label production for retail brands such as Arbella, PastaVilla, Veggipasta, CLIC, and Tamam.

Its integrated origination network buys crops directly from producers near its facilities in Canada, the United States, Türkiye, Australia, and South Africa, then processes and exports them through rail and port logistics partnerships.

The company emphasizes vertical integration—capturing value in the communities where crops are grown—and logistical advantages through bulk grain-handling agreements that connect Western Canadian farms to major railways and ports. Its Veggi line of 100% plant-based pastas, breadings, and meal kits exemplifies its focus on innovative, consumer-ready products.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pulse and grain cleaning", "Sizing and splitting", "Colour sorting", "Packaging (bulk, bagged, canned)", "Extrusion (texturized plant protein, gluten-free pasta)", "Milling (wheat semolina, pasta, rice, bulgur wheat)", "Co-packing", "Custom product mixing", "Private label production", "Bulk grain handling and transloading (truck to rail)", "Export logistics (127 countries)", "Crop origination and procurement"], "industries": ["Food ingredients", "Packaged foods", "Retail (private label/store brands)", "Agriculture (pulses, grains, specialty crops)", "International trade/export", "Food service"], "materials": ["Pulses (peas, lentils, chickpeas, beans)", "Grains (wheat, durum wheat, rice, bulgur wheat, canola, flax)", "Plant-based proteins", "Starches", "Fibres", "Flours", "Retail product ingredients (dairy, dried fruit, nuts, confectionery, oils, vinegars, blossoms)"], "equipment": ["Cleaning, sizing, splitting, colour-sorting, packaging lines", "Pasta production line (largest-capacity in the world)", "Bulgur wheat production line (largest facility in T\u00fcrkiye)", "Extrusion lines for texturized plant protein and gluten-free pasta"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated supply chain from farm to finished product", "39 state-of-the-art manufacturing facilities on five continents", "Ingredient production facilities in Minot, ND and Regina, SK", "Proprietary retail brands including Arbella, PastaVilla, Veggipasta", "Bulk grain-handling agreements with rail and port access"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered 