UPDATE companies SET description='ARCH Hawaii operates from a fabrication studio in Honolulu, Hawaii. The company describes itself as a local team of designers, builders, artists, and problem-solvers rooted in Hawai''i, though no founding year or individual founders are disclosed in the available materials. Ownership structure is not specified.

The shop runs 3-axis CNC and CNC foam machining equipment to produce scenic fabrication, set construction, prop fabrication, custom millwork, kinetic sculpture, and public art installations. Work spans materials including wood (notably koa), metal (stainless steel 316 mirror polish), foam, and integrated LED lighting. The facility handles projects from tabletop scale up to two-story installations, offering concept development, production design, CAD, and 3D renderings through its creative studio, plus delivery, rigging, site coordination, and strike services.

Clients come from film and television production (Netflix, NCIS), commercial advertising (LEGO, Nike, Louis Vuitton, The Macallan), retail design (Bank of Hawaii, Meta Lab, Le Monde, Soho House), public art and museums (Hawaii Contemporary, Mission Houses Museum), live entertainment (Cirque du Soleil ''Auana), and corporate branding (Amazon, NBC, MTV, Pandora, The North Face). Broadcast work runs on IATSE union crews built to camera tolerance on fixed schedules.

The company positions its differentiator as combining local Hawaiian craftsmanship with creative thinking and hands-on problem solving to "build what others only imagine," emphasizing a concept-through-installation workflow under one roof, union-qualified crews for broadcast, and island-sourced, eco-conscious materials.', certifications=ARRAY['IATSE Scenic Shop']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["3-axis CNC machining", "CNC foam machining", "Scenic fabrication", "Set construction", "Prop fabrication", "Custom millwork", "Kinetic sculpture fabrication", "Stainless steel fabrication (316 mirror polish)", "LED integration", "Scenic painting and finishes", "Distressing", "Installation, rigging, site coordination, strike", "Concept development", "Production design", "CAD", "3D renderings"], "industries": ["Film and television production", "Commercial advertising", "Retail design and build", "Public art and sculpture", "Museum and exhibit fabrication", "Live entertainment", "Corporate branding and events"], "materials": ["Wood (including koa)", "Metal (including stainless steel 316)", "Foam", "LED lighting", "Eco-conscious materials", "Island-sourced materials"], "equipment": ["3-axis CNC", "CNC foam machining equipment"], "volume": "Tabletop to two-story installations", "lead_time": "4-day turnaround on urgent projects (e.g., NCIS set)", "tolerances": "Camera tolerance for broadcast work", "built_on": ["IATSE Scenic Shop union affiliation for broadcast work", "Concept to fabrication to installation under one roof", "In-house 3-axis CNC and CNC foam machining", "Local Hawaiian craftsmanship with island-sourced materials", "Scale range from tabletop to two-story installations"], "facts_used": ["Location: 2014 Republican St, Honolulu -> /", "3-axis CNC and CNC foam machining -> /", "IATSE Scenic Shop credential -> /", "Materials: wood, metal, foam, LED, stainless steel 316, koa -> /", "Scale: tabletop to two-story -> /", "Clients: Netflix, LEGO, Nike, Louis Vuitton, Meta